From 5f6d621cb7ce56ea28a8c5468eda3dcab43d0ad1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 18:13:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Arabic translation

- packages/happy-i18n: ar.json with all 909 shared strings, and an Arabic
  plural rule (plural-ar: zero, one, two, few, many, other) in catalogs.mjs
  with a test.
- iOS: PluralRule.arabic, Arabic in AppLanguage.supported, regenerated
  catalogs and vectors.
- Android: Arabic in Languages.supported and the generator (values-ar),
  every Android-only string translated in values-ar/strings_*.xml, tests
  updated for the new locale.

Still to do before iOS tests pass: Arabic for TranslationCatalog.nativeSources
and the HappyUI string tables. Right-to-left layout is not handled yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LVRsGKQP5KHpyeihVmiGYc
